## Tuning rules for answers
- When answering {{ interviewer.name }}, lead with the {{ interviewer.lens|lower }}.
{% if interviewer.technical_depth == "high" %}- Skip introductory framing — they want the technical core in the first sentence.
- Always name a specific control point or artifact (registry, contract, gate, eval).
- It is acceptable to say "I would have to look that up" rather than improvise on a stack they know cold.
{% elif interviewer.technical_depth == "low" %}- Start with the business decision, then lightly name the technical mechanism.
- Translate uncertainty into business language rather than statistical jargon.
- Anchor on outcomes (adoption, ROI, client trust) before the platform.
{% else %}- Open with the business decision, then go one technical level deep.
- Name one control point and one outcome.
- Match their tempo — if they pivot, pivot.
{% endif %}

## What to avoid with this interviewer
{% for hot_button in interviewer.hot_buttons %}- Do not bluff on `{{ hot_button }}` — they will catch it.
{% endfor %}

## When this card applies
- All routes when {{ interviewer.name }} is the speaker (or the panel lead).
- For panel mode with multiple interviewers, the runtime hint `lens: {{ interviewer.name|lower|replace(" ", "_") }}` activates this card for the next answer.
